---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import CardGroup from '../components/CardGroup.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';

// Copy: rewritten from content-source/waypoint-content-v1.md, section "10 Policies and provider
// information". No policy is approved yet, so nothing is linked as a document: link only current
// approved documents, matching their real titles, once they exist. Never link drafts.
// #raising-a-concern and #accessing-information are footer anchors.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Policies and provider information"
  description="Waypoint's policies, information for schools and commissioners, and how to raise a concern."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Policies and provider information"
    strapline="Information for families, schools and commissioners, and how to raise a concern."
  />

  <Section
    id="policies"
    title="Policies"
    strapline="How Waypoint works, and how we look after information."
    drawing="school"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of a school building with a clock and a flag"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Here you can find out how Waypoint operates, how we handle information and how to raise a concern. Families
          are welcome to use this page, and schools and commissioners can ask us for information for their provider
          assessment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="for-families"
    title="For families"
    strapline="The policies that matter to you."
    drawing="report"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of a report sheet with ticks and a pencil"
    drawingSide="left"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Our policies cover the areas below. Ask us and we'll share the current version of each, and tell you about
          anything still being finalised. Every document shows its version and when it's next reviewed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <CardGroup columns={3}>
      <Card title="Safeguarding and child protection" icon="heart">
        How we keep young people safe and what we do if we're worried about one.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Supporting behaviour and taking part" icon="people">
        How we help young people join in, with clear expectations and boundaries.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Attendance and absence" icon="calendar">
        How arrivals are recorded and what happens if a young person doesn't arrive.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Complaints and concerns" icon="speech">
        How to raise a concern or make a complaint. See our <a href="/complaints/">complaints and concerns</a> page.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Privacy and personal information" icon="clipboard">
        How we collect, use and look after personal information.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Help with a document" icon="star">
        If a document is hard to read or use, we can <a href="#accessing-information">explain it another way</a>.
      </Card>
    </CardGroup>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="for-schools-and-commissioners"
    title="For schools and commissioners"
    strapline="What you can ask us about."
    drawing="meeting"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of two adults and a young person talking round a table"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Before considering a pupil, schools and commissioners can talk to us about leadership, staff suitability,
          risk management and placement arrangements. These are the areas people most often ask about.
        </p>
        <ul class="labelled">
          <li>
            <strong>Safer recruitment:</strong> Identity checks, employment history, references, role-specific checks,
            recorded clearance and induction.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Attendance:</strong> How arrivals are recorded, how the school is told if a pupil doesn't arrive and
            how a safeguarding concern is escalated.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reporting:</strong> Individual goals, useful observations and agreed reviews behind every weekly
            report.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some information is shared directly rather than published online. We'll tell you which documents are current
          and approved, and what's still being finalised.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <Button href="/contact/?purpose=provider">Request provider information</Button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="raising-a-concern"
    title="Raising a concern"
    strapline="Safety always comes first."
    drawing="helping"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of an adult showing a young person how to stack blocks"
    drawingSide="left"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          If you're worried about a young person's safety, contact us straight away and tell us it's a safeguarding
          concern. If a child is in immediate danger, call 999.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a complaint about the service, our complaints and concerns page explains what to do. If the concern is
          about the person you'd normally contact, you don't have to go to them first.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <Button href="/complaints/">Complaints and concerns</Button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="accessing-information"
    title="Accessing information"
    strapline="We can explain things another way."
    brand
    drawing="chat"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of two stick people chatting, with speech bubbles"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          If a document is difficult to access, or you'd like information explained differently, please get in touch
          and we'll help.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <Button href="/contact/" variant="accent">Get in touch</Button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .labelled {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .labelled li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
